%N A216510 Number of positive integer solutions to the equation a^2 + 6*b^2 = n.
%H A216510 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A216510/b216510.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A216510 A. Berkovich and H. Yesilyurt, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11139-009-9215-8">Ramanujan's identities and representation of integers by certain binary and quaternary quadratic forms</a>, Ramanujan J. 20 (2009), no. 3, 375-408; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0611300">arXiv:math/0611300 [math.NT]</a>. See Corollary 4.2.
%H A216510 Zhi-Hong Sun and Kenneth S. Williams, <a href="https://eudml.org/doc/278087">On the number of representations of n by ax^2 + bxy + cy^2</a>, Acta Arithmetica 122.2 (2006): 101-171. See Theorem 9.2.
%H A216510 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theta_function#Jacobi_theta_function">Jacobi theta function</a>.
%F A216510 From _David Radcliffe_, Aug 25 2026: (Start)
%F A216510 a(n) = A216513(n) - A010052(n) - A010052(6*n) + A000007(n) = (A046113(n) - 2*A010052(n) - 2*A010052(6*n) + A000007(n)) / 4.
%F A216510 G.f.: ((theta_3(0,x) - 1)*(theta_3(0,x^6) - 1))/4, where theta_3 is the third Jacobi theta function. (End)
%Y A216510 Cf. A063725, A216278, A092573, A216511, A374017.
%Y A216510 Cf. A155716, A216513 (nonnegative solutions), A046113 (integer solutions).
%Y A216510 Cf. A002481 (numbers represented by x^2 + 6*y^2).
